{
  "name": "U — retain-all with an investment case, LTV binds",
  "kind": "pipeline",
  "note": "R13 spec §19. The LTV-binding twin of t-investment-case.json: IDENTICAL scheme (same units, same rent roll, same operating lines, same programme, same take-out floors/rate/term), with only two numbers changed — cap_yield_pct 5.5 → 7.5 and takeout.ltv_cap_pct 65 → 55 — so the LTV cap falls below both coverage caps and the binding constraint flips from 'dscr' to 'ltv'. Task 11 asserts a flag fires on t- and NOT on u- (or vice versa); if both fixtures happened to bind the same way that assertion would pass for the wrong reason, which is the whole reason this fixture exists as a document distinct from its twin rather than as an override inside a single shared fixture.\n\nHAND-DERIVATION. Gross rent, occupancy and operating lines are UNCHANGED from t-investment-case.json, so stabilised NOI is identical:\n  EGR = round(295,000 × 96%) = 283,200\n  opex = round(283,200 × 10%) + round(283,200 × 2%) + 25,000 + 8,000 = 28,320 + 5,664 + 25,000 + 8,000 = 66,984\n  stabilised monthly NOI = 283,200 − 66,984 = 216,216\n  stabilised annual NOI = 12 × 216,216 = 2,594,592 pence (identical to t-investment-case.json — NOI depends on rent, occupancy and opex, none of which changed)\n\n  investment value at the WIDER 7.5% yield = round(2,594,592 × 100 / 7.5 / 1.0675)\n                    = round(259,459,200 / 7.5 / 1.0675) = round(34,594,560 / 1.0675)\n                    = round(32,407,081.97) = 32,407,082 pence (lower than t-'s 44,191,475, as a wider yield must give)\n\n  DSCR cap and ICR cap are UNCHANGED from t-investment-case.json — both are functions of NOI and the takeout's own rate/floor terms alone, and neither the NOI nor those terms moved:\n  DSCR cap = floor(2,594,592 / (1.3 × 0.0773161682)) = 25,814,005\n  ICR cap  = floor(2,594,592 / (1.3 × 0.06))          = 33,264,000\n\n  LTV cap at the NARROWER 55% cap, on the lower value = floor(32,407,082 × 55 / 100)\n                    = floor(17,823,895.10) = 17,823,895\n\n  min(17,823,895 ; 25,814,005 ; 33,264,000) = 17,823,895 = LTV cap → BINDING CONSTRAINT = 'ltv'.\n\nSee t-investment-case.json's own note for the shared programme derivation (twelve-phase network, practical_completion starting month 15, stabilisation anchored to practical_completion + 1 = month 16, ramp_months 3), the cost stack, and the same caveat about Task 3's cross-engine pinned triple using a different (two-line) operating schedule than this fixture's four.\n\nWHAT THIS FIXTURE DOES NOT COVER: as with its twin, the investment_case RESULT block does not exist until Tasks 8/11 land, so expected_metrics pins only gdv_pence and the cost_plan headline figures today; the investment-case pins (annual_noi_pence, investment_value_pence, binding_constraint = 'ltv') are deferred to Task 8 or 11.",
